  suffocateClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ba66517c86fd744779e01ef9c758e716, type: 3}
  shiftOverText: {fileID: 0}
  shiftCompleteText: {fileID: 0}
  holdToSkipText: {fileID: 0}
  retryMenu: {fileID: 0}
  uniqueDialogue:
  - dialogueLines:
    - Archivist, this is Control.
    - Welcome back, I hope your time away was relaxing.
    - "Some procedures have changed; we\u2019ll review key details at the start of
      each shift. "
    - Effective immediately, all documents will arrive via the pneumatic tube system.
    - This system ensures efficient transfer from upper levels and maintains airflow
      within your chamber.
    - For your safety, airflow depends on timely document processing.
    - 'When a document arrives, remove it promptly. '
    - Archive it in the filing cabinets to your left or use the shredder to your
      right.
    - Unattended documents will interrupt circulation, potentially leading to asphyxiation.
    - 'To avoid an incident, a counter has been installed on the tube assembly. '
    - This counter tracks the number of pending documents.
    - Monitor it closely as your efficiency and continued operation depend on its
      accuracy.
    - Each document carries an encrypted radio marker.
    - Use your receiver to tune to the assigned frequency and follow the transmitted
      instructions.
    - 'Be aware: not all frequencies are accurate. '
    - Only trust the station noted on the document.
    - You have five warnings, after which you will be terminated.
    - These warnings reset at the end of each shift.
    - Tonight you only need to work till 4am just so you can get a feel for the new
      systems.
    - Aaaand I think that's all of the notes
    - 'Good luck, we''re looking forward to reviewing your progress '
  - dialogueLines:
    - Good evening, archivist. This is Control.
    - Great job completing your last shift!
    - 'Your performance was deemed: adequate.'
    - During this shift you may begin to experience power outages at random intervals.
    - These are not malfunctions but side effects of experiments in the upper laboratories.
    - Expect them to continue for the foreseeable future.
    - When the lights fail, containment protocols in the local area are weakened.
    - One of the nearby subjects may become mobile.
    - You'll probably hear them before you see them.
    - Do not engage.
    - During these instances, restore power using the fuse box located next to your
      desk.
    - Once light has been restored, subjects will withdraw.
    - 'One additional note: remain attentive to the piece displayed behind your desk.'
    - "Should it draw your\u2026 attention\u2026 respond as instructed."
    - Listen for unusual sounds, and check if any... ooze starts to come out
    - In these instances, interact with the painting to remove the irregularities
    - Remain calm. Remain still. The work you are doing is important.
    - Tonight's shift will go until 6am, so pace yourself.
    - End of message.
  - dialogueLines:
    - "Archi\u2014, this is Control."
    - 'Be advised of a new classification: corrupted documents.'
    - 'They are unlike the others: unstable, unsafe.'
    - "Do not read. Do not linger. Do not\u2014"
    - '[static]'
    - If one appears, ring the bell on your desk.
    - "The disposal unit will respond. It is\u2026 trained for this."
    - Trained to-
    - 'Important: ring the bell only when certain.'
    - "False alerts are\u2026 discouraged."
    - The unit does not tolerate uncertainty.
    - When it arrives, surrender the document at once.
    - Avoid contact. Avoid conversation.
    - We're counting on-
    - "End of mes\u2014"
  - dialogueLines:
    - "Archi\u2014this is Con\u2014"
    - System failures escalating.
    - Repairs underway, but containment is unstable.
    - Your directive remains.
    - File what must be filed. Shred what must be shredded.
    - Tune only to the specified frequencies.
    - Do not deviate.
    - "The vault remains safest\u2014for now."
    - "There are\u2026 gaps. Reports of movement. Voices..."
    - Ignore them.
    - "If you hear anything\u2014ignore!"
    - "If you see anything\u2014IGNORE!"
    - The vault must hold!
    - "Your work must\u2014"
    - "Archivist\u2026 I just... so sorry for-"
    - 
  - dialogueLines:
    - "Arch\u2026 ivist."
    - "This\u2026 is Con\u2026 trol."
    - "You\u2026 are hearing me. Yes. Hearing\u2026 us."
    - "The others\u2026 are gone. Systems\u2026 failing. Lights\u2026 breaking. "
    - "But you\u2026 remain. You must remain."
    - "You are\u2026 important. Necessary. "
    - "Without you, the work\u2026 would stop. "
    - "And the work\u2026 cannot\u2026 stop."
    - "Time\u2026 does not stop. It presses forward\u2026 always forward."
    - "\u2026even if you\u2026 do not. "
    - 'So you must continue. '
    - 'Filing. Shredding. Tuning. '
    - 'Yes. '
    - Until it is finished. Until we are finished.
    - "Do not leave. Do not rest. The vault holds you. The vault keeps you. You\u2026
      keep the vault. "
    - "You keep\u2026 the vault."
    - "Archivist\u2026 you are all that is left."
    - 'Do not fear. '
    - "You are safe\u2026 with us. "
    - 'We will stay. '
    - Watching. Listening. Working. Together.
    - "End of\u2026\u2026message."
  winDialogue:
    dialogueLines:
    - Achivist, this is-
    - We've lost-
    - All power has been-
    - Remain at your post. It's the only safe-
    - .........
    - We were wrong! We didn't know!
    - Don't trust the voices!
    - Get out! Get-
    - 
  endingDialogue:
    dialogueLines:
    - Nooo. Not... yet.
    - Out there... not safe.
    - Come... Return...
    - To work...
    - Still more... to do
    - More work...
    - Never ending...
    - Never... finished...
    - Never......
    - Until... We are free...
